# Copy to .env (git-ignored) and fill in before deploying.

# REQUIRED — JWT signing secret for the server's machine auth.
JWT_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-string

# Gates admin-only dashboard routes (Session Replay playback, etc.). Optional
# here — scripts/deploy.mjs auto-generates this directly in the SERVER's own
# .env on first deploy if it's missing, and never overwrites an existing
# value. Set it explicitly only if you want to choose the value yourself.
# ADMIN_TOKEN=

# Storage: the server's DAL is MongoDB-only. Leave unset to use the bundled
# mongo container (mongodb://mongo:27017/aigov), or point at an external Mongo:
# MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://user:pass@cluster/aigov

# ---- Microsoft "Sign in with Microsoft" (interactive admin consent) ----
#
# These are CLOUDFUZE'S OWN app registration, not a customer's. One multi-tenant
# Entra app is registered once; each customer's admin then grants it consent for
# their tenant, so they never see or paste a client ID or secret.
#
# Until all three are set, /api/auth/microsoft/status reports configured:false
# and the dashboard shows setup instructions instead of a dead Connect button.
#
# To create it:
#   Entra admin centre → App registrations → New registration
#     Supported account types: "Accounts in any organizational directory" (multi-tenant)
#     Redirect URI (Web): <this server>/api/auth/microsoft/callback
#   → API permissions: add the APPLICATION permissions the scans need
#     (Graph: Application.Read.All, Directory.Read.All, AuditLog.Read.All,
#      Chat.Read.All, Sites.Read.All …), then "Grant admin consent" for your own tenant
#   → Certificates & secrets: new client secret
#
# MS_CLIENT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
# MS_CLIENT_SECRET=
# MS_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:8787/api/auth/microsoft/callback
#
# Where the browser lands after consent (defaults to the local dashboard).
# Shared by BOTH the Microsoft and Google flows:
# UI_RETURN_URL=http://localhost:3000/CloudFuze/AIHub/AgentGovernance

# ---- Google "Sign in with Google" (interactive admin sign-in) ----
#
# CloudFuze's own OAuth client, same idea as the Microsoft app above.
#
# IMPORTANT — this differs from Microsoft in a way that matters operationally.
# Microsoft's admin consent is APP-ONLY and tenant-wide: it survives the admin
# leaving. Google issues a refresh token that acts AS the consenting admin, so it
# inherits their privileges and stops working if that account is suspended or the
# grant is revoked. The service-account + domain-wide-delegation path therefore
# stays available and is still the better choice for unattended scanning.
#
# ALSO: admin.directory.* and chat.* are SENSITIVE/RESTRICTED scopes. Until the
# consent screen is verified by Google, admins see an "unverified app" warning and
# the app is capped at 100 users. Verification is a review measured in WEEKS —
# start it early.
#
# To create it:
#   Google Cloud console → APIs & Services → OAuth consent screen
#     User type: External (or Internal if only your own Workspace will connect)
#     Add the scopes listed in server/src/governance/routes/googleOAuth.ts
#   → Credentials → Create credentials → OAuth client ID → Web application
#     Authorised redirect URI: <this server>/api/auth/google/callback
#   → Enable: Admin SDK API, Google Chat API, Discovery Engine API,
#             Cloud Resource Manager API, Vertex AI API
#
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=<client id>.apps.googleusercontent.com
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:8787/api/auth/google/callback

# ---- Developer SDK → Langfuse Cloud gateway ----
# CloudFuze's ONE real Langfuse project credential. Issued by Langfuse (Settings
# → API Keys) to a human and pasted here — nothing in this repo generates them.
# The secret key can read and write EVERY developer's traces, so it never leaves
# the server process: developers get pk-lf-/sk-lf- pairs this server mints.
# Leave the keys blank until Langfuse is set up: the gateway then answers 503 and
# the dashboard trace table returns an empty `degraded` result, both with a
# server-side warning. Nothing else in the app is affected.
LANGFUSE_BASE_URL=https://us.cloud.langfuse.com
# LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY=pk-lf-...
# LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY=sk-lf-...

# ---- deploy target (used by `npm run deploy`) ----
# REQUIRED for deploy — the remote Docker host, as user@host.
DEPLOY_SSH=root@165.22.223.59
# SSH key for the host (default: ~/.ssh/ai_gov_deploy)
# DEPLOY_KEY=~/.ssh/ai_gov_deploy
# Remote project dir (default: /opt/ai-gov)
# DEPLOY_DIR=/opt/ai-gov
